WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.840
Chapter seven: discussion and annotations.

00:00:02.840 --> 00:00:05.681
Every listed paper has an open discussion.

00:00:05.681 --> 00:00:13.925
Unlike formal reviews, discussion is open to any member, it is informal, and it never changes the status of a paper.

00:00:13.925 --> 00:00:16.865
Anyone can read discussions and annotations.

00:00:16.865 --> 00:00:21.941
To post, reply, annotate or vote, you need tier one, Member, or above.

00:00:21.941 --> 00:00:26.658
Open the Discussion tab on a paper, or the discussion page of the paper.

00:00:26.658 --> 00:00:30.661
Start a thread, or reply to any post. Replies can nest.

00:00:30.661 --> 00:00:35.396
A post can have up to 4,000 characters. Choose Sign and submit to post.

00:00:35.396 --> 00:00:40.064
Every post is a signed record, like everything else on Scholium.

00:00:40.064 --> 00:00:44.496
You cannot edit or delete a post after you submit it. So write with care.

00:00:44.496 --> 00:00:48.197
You can mark the post of another member as helpful, once per post.

00:00:48.197 --> 00:00:52.299
You cannot vote on your own posts, and you cannot withdraw a vote.

00:00:52.299 --> 00:00:55.440
Helpful votes only change the order of the thread.

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:58.645
The most helpful posts come first, then the oldest.

00:00:58.645 --> 00:01:04.197
Votes never show as counts on papers, and they never affect the status of a paper.

00:01:04.197 --> 00:01:09.419
An annotation is a comment attached to one paragraph of one version of a paper.

00:01:09.419 --> 00:01:14.688
To add one, click a paragraph in the reading view, or move to it with Tab. Press A.

00:01:14.688 --> 00:01:20.229
Write your note and choose Save annotation. Escape closes the box without saving.

00:01:20.229 --> 00:01:25.175
Annotations appear as markers beside the paragraph, and in the Discussion tab.

00:01:25.175 --> 00:01:28.535
If a paper has none yet, you see: No annotations yet.

00:01:28.535 --> 00:01:31.979
Select a paragraph and press A to add the first.

00:01:31.979 --> 00:01:37.303
An annotation attaches to the whole paragraph. You cannot select part of a sentence.

00:01:37.303 --> 00:01:39.458
Annotations belong to one version.

00:01:39.458 --> 00:01:43.280
A new version of the paper starts without annotations.

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:47.840
If a moderator hides an annotation, it shows Hidden by moderation.

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:53.317
Every post has a Report action. Chapter nine explains how to report content.

00:01:53.317 --> 00:01:56.485
Posts and votes count toward your daily write limit.

00:01:56.485 --> 00:02:01.968
When you reach it, a message tells you that you are going too fast, and when to try again.

00:02:01.968 --> 00:02:04.683
Chapter two explains the daily limits.

00:02:04.683 --> 00:02:09.718
In short: anyone can read, and members can post, reply, annotate and vote.

00:02:09.718 --> 00:02:14.072
Posts are signed and final. Helpful votes only order the thread.

00:02:14.072 --> 00:02:17.747
An annotation belongs to one paragraph of one version.

00:02:17.747 --> 00:02:20.528
Next, chapter eight: AI pre-review.
